 "review": "Independent, read-only: OK — the same resources stay alive (the display backend's weak lookup still tells .released from .owner), nothing read the earlier cursors, rollback unchanged, the bitmap/menu-graphics/lifecycle histories only grow in tests. Fixed from it: a deterministic release order (insertion order instead of a dictionary's hash order), one pass over the receipts, the test now shows that either holder alone keeps its resources, the count joins the runtime-menu test's hash and fingerprint, card links.",
 "boundaries": [
  "Resources are still kept until the session ends (as before); only their iterations' requests and replies are no longer kept",
  "The soak's VS session is virtual-clock; the menus are real-clock"
 ]
